622067523.en:
@_**Nia|571657** [said](https://rust-lang.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/219381-t-libs/topic/CovariantUnsafeCell/near/622066139):
```quote
i don't believe we offer any way to have a named generic param that we're bivariant over
```
We do, but only if it appears in an associated type bound:
```
trait Hmm {
    type Assoc;
}
type A = fn(&&i32);
type B = for<'a> fn(&'a &'a i32);

impl Hmm for A {
    type Assoc = i32;
}
impl Hmm for B {
    type Assoc = u32;
}

struct Test<T: Hmm<Assoc = U>, U>(T);

pub fn main() {
    let x: Test<A, i32> = Test(|_| {});
    let x: Test<B, u32> = x;
    let x: Test<A, i32> = x;
}
```

