Yeah I did see that - [`TokenStream::expand_expr`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/proc_macro/struct.TokenStream.html#method.expand_expr), right? That's something I thought about, but honestly I'm not sure I like that as a solution, where I would write something like
```rust
#[proc_macro]
pub fn callback(input: TokenStream) -> TokenStream {
    let Callback { run, callback } = match parse_callback_from(input) {
        Ok(callback) => callback,
        Err(err) => return parse_compile_err(err),
    };
    let expanded = match run.expand_expr() {
        Ok(expanded) => expanded,
        Err(err) => return expand_compile_err(err),
    };
    expand_callback_with_input(callback, expanded)
}
```
My biggest reason for not liking it is that it makes a callback take two expansions instead of one, and for the awful nightmare projects I like to work on that's kind of a nonstarter.

I've found the callback pattern to be very useful in `macro_rules!` land, so I was hoping that there might be something along those lines that would be possible in order to support that.

