617848653.en:
If `WRef` still works equivalently to a `&mut` with reborrowing then no: once you reborrow and pass a `WRef` copy into a function, the original `WRef` is disabled until the function return value is dropped (if it captures the `'a` lifetime).

eg.
```rust
fn foo(a: &mut u32) -> &u32 {
  a
}

fn main() {
  let a = &mut 0u32;
  let b = foo(a);
  core::ptr::eq(a, b); // err: can't use a because it is still borrowed in b
}
```

