620038969.en:
The type of the reference is irrelevant here. The subobject provenance restriction happens at the point where the field projection happens. A reference which has permissions to access outside its type and one which doesn't have the same Rust type, they just have different provenance.

This means that specifying  whether a field projection gets subobject provenance should be done with an attribute on the field itself:

```rust
struct Foo {
    #[header]
   header: u8,

    field: u8,
    ...
}

// x has permissions to access all of Foo.
let x = &foo.header;

// y only has permissions to access the u8 field.
let y = &foo.field;
```

